	Greetings netlanders.

	Well after trying to make the "official overlay version" on my PC,
here's a few hints/comments.


	MAKE:
	I was using NDMAKE 4.5.  If you don't have this program and would
like to try to get a copy of this program, try this:

Send the mail message:

Subject:/PDGET PD:<MSDOS.C>NDMAKE45.ARC
/PDGET PD:<MSDOS.C>NDMAKE45.ARC
<EOT>

to listserv@vm1.nodak.edu

This is a method of requesting the file from the simtel archive.  You (if
all is working well) should recieve a ~7 part message that is the uuencoded
file as return mail.
NOTE: the checksums on these files (i find) are usually incorrect, but they
still uudecode properly.

	When running the make I had ~585k free and seemed to have no memory
problems.


	COMPILER:

lev_comp.c:
	The lev_comp.c that was distributed was not consistent with the
lev_comp.y that was distributed.  If you can use a "yacc" of some kind to 
generate your lev_comp.c from lev_comp.y.  If this is impossible, all you
need to do to get the compile to work is to change all occurances of "dig"
(not "ndig" *just* "dig") to "digpos" in the file lev_comp.c.  However,
this may not reflect other changes to lev_comp.y made for this patchlevel
release.

termlib.lib:
	The termcap.uu distributed may still leave the "H"s all over the
screen.  If it does, mail me and I can send you the updated "fix"ed version
that mike threepoint posted a while back.

	The rest was just as described in Install.dos.


	EXECUTEABLE:

777706 Bytes.  Runs fine in ~520k. (Better in more......)

